# Google Analytics on HTML pages

When creating or publishing a new HTML page, add Google Analytics at the **start of `<head>`** (before meta charset is fine).

## Snippet (adjust `gtag-config.js` path by directory depth)

```html
  <!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-YJDKH6WYT1"></script>
  <script src="PATH_TO/assets/js/gtag-config.js"></script>
```

| Page location | `gtag-config.js` path |
|---------------|------------------------|
| Site root (`index.html`, `about.html`, …) | `assets/js/gtag-config.js` |
| One level down (`notes/`, `research/`) | `../assets/js/gtag-config.js` |
| Two levels down (`notes/maritime/`) | `../../assets/js/gtag-config.js` |

Measurement ID is configured in `assets/js/gtag-config.js` (`G-YJDKH6WYT1`). Do not duplicate `gtag("config", …)` inline unless intentionally changing that file.

## Checklist

- New English page + Traditional Chinese pair: add GA to **both** files.
- Redirect-only pages (e.g. `index.en.html`): include GA as well.
- Copy from an existing page in the **same folder** to get the correct relative path.
